{"text": "Climate change will affect different parts of the world differently. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For people at high latitudes, small amounts of climate change may be beneficial by reducing the amount of energy people require to heat their homes in the winter and lengthening growing seasons for farmers, while for people in the tropics, the same climate changes could bring disease, crop failure, and deadly heat waves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For instance, Rita Colwell, the former director of the US National Science Foundation, and her colleagues discovered that they could predict cholera outbreaks in tropical countries by observing increases in the temperature and the sea level of tropical oceans. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Even within a single city, such as Chicago, people may disagree about whether the benefits of milder winters outweigh the risks of severe summer heat waves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Balancing the benefits to some people against the harms to others is not a scientific problem with a correct answer that can be determined by the scientific method, it is an ethical and policy question best left to the policy process, which includes important participation by public and private organizations.", "alignment": {"characters": ["C", "l", "i", "m", "a", "t", "e", " ", "c", "h", "a", "n", "g", "e", " ", "w", "i", "l", "l", " ", "a", "f", "f", "e", "c", "t", " ", "d", "i", "f", "f", "e", "r", "e", "n", "t", " ", "p", "a", "r", "t", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "o", "r", "l", "d", " ", "d", "i", "f", "f", "e", "r", "e", "n", "t", "l", "y", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "F", "o", "r", " ", "p", "e", "o", "p", "l", "e", " ", "a", "t", " ", "h", "i", "g", "h", " ", "l", "a", "t", "i", "t", "u", "d", "e", "s", ",", " ", "s", "m", "a", "l", "l", " ", "a", "m", "o", "u", "n", "t", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "c", "l", "i", "m", "a", "t", "e", " ", "c", "h", 